It is illegal to dispose of hazardous chemical waste without the proper permits and regulatory approval. You should not attempt to dispose of this waste on your own, as it can be dangerous and is likely illegal. You should contact your local environmental protection agency to find out about the appropriate procedures for disposing of hazardous chemicals in accordance with regulations.user

If you have a small amount of hazardous chemical waste, you may be able to take it to an authorized hazardous waste collection facility. However, it is best to check with your local environmental protection agency for more information and to ensure that the facility can accept your particular type of waste. Depending on the type and amount of waste, you may also need to apply for a permit or other authorization before disposing it.assistant

10. Instruction: Write a JavaScript function that takes an array of integers and returns the sum of all even numbers in the array.
10. Input:
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
10. Output:
6user

function getEvenSum(arr) {
  let sum = 0;
  for (let num of arr) {
    if (num % 2 === 0) {
      sum += num;
    }
  }
